<title>BELGIUM: EU wheat tax to be approved on May 7.</title>
<headline>EU wheat tax to be approved on May 7.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A European Union tax on soft wheat exports is due to be formally approved and enter into force on Wednesday, a European Commission official said.</p>
<p>The official said that the 15 Ecus a tonne tax on daily exports of soft wheat grain and 20 Ecus a tonne on wheat flour would be approved without discussion under the EU's so-called written procedure.</p>
<p>On April 24, the EU cereals management committee, made up of delegates from member states, supported the move, which is aimed at saving supplies for domestic consumers and dampening prices.</p>
<p>Exporters who have taken out nil value export licences will be liable to tax if they have not customs cleared their grain and flour exports before the decision takes effect.</p>
<p>--Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
